        "date": "2026-11-22T15:58:41Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(xtask): cover a package-level link in the unit sweep and fold link-target case on mac\n\nTwo gaps in the gate unit sweep (#3173):\n\n- The scan skipped a link at the package level, but no test covered it.\n  New test: a package link (whose name differs only by case) is never\n  entered, the sweep removes nothing through it, and the link stays.\n- norm() folded case only on Windows. On the case-insensitive default\n  volume of macOS, a canonicalized link target that differs only by case\n  missed the process-check needles. norm() now folds case on macOS too.\n\nThe verdict logic of the sweep is untouched.\n\nFixes #3173",
